# ── Always required ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Database connection string. Local dev: SQLite file (already the default
# below). Production: a PostgreSQL connection string - see README
# "Switching to PostgreSQL" for exact Neon/Supabase setup steps.
DATABASE_URL="file:./dev.db"

# Only needed alongside DATABASE_URL when your PostgreSQL provider uses a
# connection pooler (Neon, Supabase): DATABASE_URL is the pooled connection
# used at runtime, DIRECT_URL is the direct connection Prisma Migrate needs.
# Leave unset for SQLite.
# DIRECT_URL="postgresql://..."

# Signs login session tokens is NOT used for that anymore (sessions are
# database-backed, see src/lib/session.ts) but is still checked at startup
# as a general application secret. Must be at least 32 random characters.
# Generate one with: openssl rand -base64 32
SESSION_SECRET="dev-only-change-me-to-a-long-random-string-32chars+"

# ── Required in production only (local dev has working fallbacks) ───────

# Full public URL of the deployed app, no trailing slash. Used to build
# absolute links in emails (password reset, verification) and page metadata.
# APP_URL="https://webg.co.il"

# Transactional email (Resend: https://resend.com). Without this, dev mode
# logs the email content (including reset/verify links) to the server
# console instead of crashing - nothing is sent, nothing is lost.
# RESEND_API_KEY="re_xxxxxxxxxxxx"
# EMAIL_FROM="WEBG <no-reply@yourdomain.com>"

# Cloudflare R2 (S3-compatible object storage) for uploaded images. Without
# these, uploads are written to a local ./uploads folder - fine for
# development, but that folder does not persist on serverless hosting, so
# all five are required whenever NODE_ENV=production (enforced at startup
# by src/lib/env.ts).
# R2_ACCOUNT_ID="..."
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID="..."
# R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY="..."
# R2_BUCKET_NAME="webg-uploads"
# R2_PUBLIC_URL="https://pub-xxxxxxxx.r2.dev"

# ── Optional ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Comma-separated emails allowed into the private /admin platform dashboard
# (see src/lib/admin.ts). Unset or empty means nobody can reach it - never
# left enabled by accident on a fresh deploy.
# ADMIN_EMAILS="owner@example.com,cofounder@example.com"

# SMS for phone verification codes (Global SMS). Phone verification turns on only when BOTH are set;
# SMS_SENDER must be the sender name Global SMS approved (or the account's virtual number).
# GLOBALSMS_API_KEY=""
# SMS_SENDER=""

# Cloudflare Turnstile ("not a robot", usually no click) on the public site forms - see src/lib/turnstile.ts.
# On only when both are set; add webg.co.il as the widget's hostname in Cloudflare. The site key is public
# and built into the page, so a change needs a redeploy; the secret key is Vercel only.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=""
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=""

# Payments (HYP Pay - see src/lib/payments and src/server/billing.ts). Billing turns on only when all three
# are set (Vercel only - KEY and PassP are secrets); without them publishing and Pro cost nothing. In the HYP
# portal, set the success URL to https://<APP_URL>/api/billing/return and keep "show errors on the payment page".
# HYP_MASOF=""
# HYP_KEY=""
# HYP_PASSP=""
# Development/tests only: a fake gateway with a local payment page (/dev/fake-hyp). Ignored in production.
# PAYMENTS_FAKE="1"
# Protects the daily billing job (/api/cron/billing, scheduled in vercel.json). Vercel Cron sends it automatically.
# CRON_SECRET=""

# Error reporting (Sentry) - set on Vercel only, so local development never reports. Without the DSN
# nothing is sent. SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN (secret) lets the build upload source maps, so errors show the
# real line of code; SENTRY_ORG / SENTRY_PROJECT are the slugs from the Sentry project settings.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=""
# SENTRY_ORG=""
# SENTRY_PROJECT=""
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=""
